// GENERATED — the three faces the reading-list cover is set in, base64'd.
//
// Baloo 2 (headings) and Outfit (body) are the design system's own faces, the same two
// `@charcuterie/tokens` ships and `web/src/styles/app.css` loads. SIL OFL, which is what
// lets them live in a public repo at all.
//
// WHY THE BYTES ARE IN A SOURCE FILE and not a `.ttf` next to it: the runtime image carries
// ONLY `server/dist/index.js` (see the Dockerfile's stage 3) and the esbuild bundle
// externalizes nothing, so anything read off disk at runtime is a file that is not in the
// image. Inlining is also the only form that works identically under `tsx` in dev and the
// bundle in prod, with no loader config in either.
//
// WHY NOT THE WOFF2 @charcuterie/tokens ALREADY SHIPS: Satori parses TTF/OTF/WOFF and not
// WOFF2, and decompressing those woff2 yields a VARIABLE font whose `name` table Google
// subset away — satori's opentype fork throws on its `fvar` axis names. Static per-weight
// TTFs from Google Fonts, subset to latin, are what parse.
//
// How these were made (one-time; re-run only to change a face or add a weight):
//
//   curl -s "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Baloo+2:wght@700&family=Outfit:wght@400;600"
//   # Node's default UA gets TrueType back — a browser UA would get woff2. Download each
//   # .ttf the sheet names, then subset to latin and base64 it:
//   npm i subset-font
//   node -e "..." # subsetFont(ttf, latinChars, { targetFormat: 'truetype' })
//
// Latin only, deliberately: Baloo 2's full static TTF is 418 KB because it carries
// Devanagari, and a queue label in this house is English.

